167-0a2fa6420467:d02", "start": 670, "end": 807, "text": "The novel's success led to discussions about potential adaptations, but it remains a celebrated piece of literature in its original form."}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0167-0a2fa6420467:d03", "start": 0, "end": 108, "text": "Monkey Grip (novel) Monkey Grip is a 1977 novel by Australian writer Helen Garner, her first published book."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0167-0a2fa6420467:d03", "start": 109, "end": 232, "text": "It initially received a mixed critical reception, but has now become accepted as a classic of modern Australian literature."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0167-0a2fa6420467:d03", "start": 233, "end": 483, "text": "The novel deals with the life of single-mother Nora, as she narrates her increasingly tumultuous romantic relationship with a flaky heroin addict, juxtaposed with her raising a daughter while living in share houses in Melbourne during the late 1970s."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0167-0a2fa6420467:d03", "start": 484, "end": 559, "text": "A film based on the novel, also titled \"Monkey Grip\", was released in 1982."}, "D4S5": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0167-0a2fa6420467:d03", "start": 560, "end": 627, "text": "In the 1990s, when critics identified the Australian literary genre"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0167-0a2fa6420467:d04", "start": 0, "end": 27, "text": "The Sydney Morning Herald ."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0167-0a2fa6420467:d04", "start": 28, "end": 53, "text": "Retrieved 13 April 2016 ."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0167-0a2fa6420467:d04", "start": 54, "end": 162, "text": "^ Goldsworthy , Kerryn ( 1996 ) Australian Writers : Helen Garner , Melbourne , Oxford University Press , p."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0167-0a2fa6420467:d04", "start": 163, "end": 201, "text": "28 ^ Vernav , Jean-François ( 2016 ) ."}, "D5S5": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0167-0a2fa6420467:d04", "start": 202, "end": 240, "text": "A Brief Take on the Australian Novel ."}, "D5S6": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0167-0a2fa6420467:d04", "start": 241, "end": 289, "text": "Wakefield Press ( Adelaide , South Australia ) ."}, "D5S7": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0167-0a2fa6420467:d04", "start": 290, "end": 292, "text": "p."}, "D5S8": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0167-0a2fa6420467:d04", "start": 293, "end": 298, "text": "127 ."}, "D5S9": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0167-0a2fa6420467:d04", "start": 299, "end": 323, "text": "ISBN 978-1-74305-404-8 ."}, "D5S10": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0167-0a2fa6420467:d04", "start": 324, "end": 375, "text": "^ `` On the ruthless honesty of 'Monkey Grip ' `` ."}, "D5S11": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0167-0a2fa6420467:d04", "start": 376, "end": 389, "text": "The Monthly ."}, "D5S12": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0167-0a2fa6420467:d04", "start": 390, "end": 402, "text": "April 2022 ."}, "D5S13": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0167-0a2fa6420467:d04", "start": 403, "end": 427, "text": "Retrieved 17 June 2022 ."}, "D5S14": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0167-0a2fa6420467:d04", "start": 428, "end": 453, "text": "^ Goldsworthy ( 1996 ) p."}, "D5S15": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0167-0a2fa6420467:d04", "start": 454, "end": 479, "text": "1 ^ a b Brennan 2017 , p."}, "D5S16": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0167-0a2fa6420467:d04", "start": 480, "end": 482, "text": "45"}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0167-0a2fa6420467:d05", "start": 0, "end": 52, "text": "Reception [ edit ] The film received mixed reviews ."}, "D6S2": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0167-0a2fa6420467:d05", "start": 53, "end": 187, "text": "Helen Garner , who wrote the novel upon which the film was based , 